<Base title="Measurement Methodology and Sources | CupToGram" description="Learn how CupToGram estimates ingredient weights and why measurements can vary." path="/methodology/"><main class="wrap content"><h1>Measurement methodology</h1><p>Ingredient conversion values are reference estimates, not exact physical constants. They can vary with brand, particle size, moisture, temperature, settling, and the technique used to fill a measuring cup.</p><h2>How to use the values</h2><ul><li>For flour and fine powders, fluff first, spoon into the cup, and level without packing unless the recipe says otherwise.</li><li>For brown sugar, follow the recipe's packing instruction.</li><li>For liquids, use a liquid measuring jug on a level surface.</li><li>For baking precision, prefer grams measured with a kitchen scale.</li></ul><h2>Verification status</h2><p>Initial values are provisional and marked for review in the site's data source. They must be checked against a consistent, authoritative ingredient-weight reference before launch. Ranges indicate practical measurement variation. Do not treat these estimates as nutrition, medical, or food-safety advice.</p></main></Base>